it to the government of then-Kiirun City.","wpu":"Zhongzheng Park (Keelung)","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/79/CKS_Park_7_070405.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Xian Dong Yan","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.145222,"lo":121.748389,"d":1600,"ds":"Xian Dong Yan (仙洞巖), literally Immortal cave, is a natural sea cave in Zhongshan District, Keelung, Taiwan. It is a designated Cultural Landscape by the Bureau of Cultural Heritage in Taiwan. The cave was a shrine and resting place for fishermen during Qing dynasty period and was converted into a Buddhist Temple during the Japanese colonial period.","wpu":"Xian Dong Yan","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/%E4%BB%99%E6%B4%9E%E5%B7%96%E5%B1%B1%E9%96%80.jpg/960px-%E4%BB%99%E6%B4%9E%E5%B7%96%E5%B1%B1%E9%96%80.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Ershawan Battery","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.1375,"lo":121.7575,"d":1831,"ds":"Ershawan Battery (traditional Chinese: 二沙灣砲臺; simplified Chinese: 二沙湾炮台; pinyin: Èrshāwān Pàotái), or better known as Tenable Gate of the Sea (Chinese: 海門天險; Wade–Giles: hai-men-tien-hsien) is a battery emplacements camp in Zhongzheng District, Keelung, Taiwan. It was built during Taiwan's Qing era and was the site of combat between the French and Chinese forces during the Sino-French War.","wpu":"Ershawan Battery","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Ershawan_Battery_IMG_1781_%283392540293%29.jpg/960px-Ershawan_Battery_IMG_1781_%283392540293%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Holy Trinity Church (Keelung)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.127665,"lo":121.757777,"d":1885,"ds":"Holy Trinity Church, Keelung (Chinese: 基隆聖三一堂), is a Protestant church located at t No. 163 Tung Ming Road, Hsinyi District, Keelung, an important port city in northern Taiwan. It belongs to the Taiwan Episcopal Church.","wpu":"Holy Trinity Church (Keelung)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Holy_Trinity_Episcopal_Church%2C_Keelung_-_Outside_1.jpg/960px-Holy_Trinity_Episcopal_Church%2C_Keelung_-_Outside_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Keelung Fort Commander's Official Residence","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.140417,"lo":121.758167,"d":2006,"ds":"The Keelung Fort Commander's Official Residence (Chinese: 基隆要塞司令官邸; pinyin: Jīlóng Yàosài Sīlìng Guāndǐ) is a former residence in Zhongzheng District, Keelung City, Taiwan.","wpu":"Keelung Fort Commander's Official Residence","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/%E7%99%BD%E5%A4%A9%E7%9A%84%E5%9F%BA%E9%9A%86%E8%A6%81%E5%A1%9E%E5%8F%B8%E4%BB%A4%E9%83%A8%E5%AE%98%E9%82%B8.jpg/960px-%E7%99%BD%E5%A4%A9%E7%9A%84%E5%9F%BA%E9%9A%86%E8%A6%81%E5%A1%9E%E5%8F%B8%E4%BB%A4%E9%83%A8%E5%AE%98%E9%82%B8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Baimiweng Fort","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.155556,"lo":121.743111,"d":2527,"ds":"The Baimiweng Fort (traditional Chinese: 白米甕砲台; simplified Chinese: 白米瓮炮台; pinyin: Báimǐwèng Pàotái), also known as Holland Castle or Gun Emplacement of Fort Holland, is a former fort in Zhongshan District, Keelung, Taiwan.","wpu":"Baimiweng Fort","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Baimiwong_fort_%28%E7%99%BD%E7%B1%B3%E7%94%95%E7%A0%B2%E5%8F%B0%29_%2811313783914%29.jpg/960px-Baimiwong_fort_%28%E7%99%BD%E7%B1%B3%E7%94%95%E7%A0%B2%E5%8F%B0%29_%2811313783914%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Embrace Cultural and Creative Park","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.112222,"lo":121.757194,"d":2886,"ds":"The Embrace Cultural and Creative Park (traditional Chinese: 擁恆文創園區; simplified Chinese: 拥恒文创园区; pinyin: Yōnghéng Wénchuàng Yuánqū) is a multi-purpose park in Xinyi District, Keelung, Taiwan.","wpu":"Embrace Cultural and Creative Park","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Memory_Collections_Hall%2C_Embrace_Cultural_and_Creative_Park_20160404.jpg/960px-Memory_Collections_Hall%2C_Embrace_Cultural_and_Creative_Park_20160404.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Nuannuan Ande Temple","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.102083,"lo":121.738583,"d":3440,"ds":"The Nuannuan Ande Temple (Chinese: 暖暖安德宮; pinyin: Nuǎnnuǎn Āndé Gōng) is a temple in Nuannuan District, Keelung, Taiwan. The temple is dedicated to the sea goddess Mazu, the patron deity of fishermen, sailors, and any marine-related occupations. The temple is an important and prominent place of worship in Nuannuan District.","wpu":"Nuannuan Ande Temple","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Nuannuan_Ande_Temple_20120304.jpg/960px-Nuannuan_Ande_Temple_20120304.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Heping Island Park","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.161,"lo":121.763944,"d":3937,"ds":"Heping Island Park (Chinese: 和平島公園; pinyin: Hépíng Dǎo Gōngyuán) is a park in Heping Island, Zhongzheng District, Keelung, Taiwan.","wpu":"Heping Island Park","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Heping_Island_Park_07.23.jpg/960px-Heping_Island_Park_07.23.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Dawulun Fort","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.158667,"lo":121.708944,"d":4232,"ds":"The Dawulun Fort, also Ta Wu Lun Fort, (traditional Chinese: 大武崙砲台, 大武崙礮臺; simplified Chinese: 大武仑炮台, 大武仑礮台; pinyin: Dàwǔlún Pàotái; Wade–Giles: Ta4-wu3-lun2 P'ao4-t'ai2) is a former fort on Mount Dawulun (Ta-wu-lun, Dia buron), Anle District, Keelung, Taiwan.","wpu":"Dawulun Fort","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Dawulun_Fort_IMG_1867_%283396467292%29.jpg/960px-Dawulun_Fort_IMG_1867_%283396467292%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Gongzi Liao Fort","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.144528,"lo":121.78025,"d":4249,"ds":"The Gongzi Liao Fort (traditional Chinese: 槓子寮砲台; simplified Chinese: 杠子寮炮台; pinyin: Gàngzi Liáo Pàotái) is a former fort in Xinyi District, Keelung, Taiwan.","wpu":"Gongzi Liao Fort","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/%E6%A7%93%E5%AD%90%E5%AF%AE%E7%A0%B2%E5%8F%B0-03.JPG/960px-%E6%A7%93%E5%AD%90%E5%AF%AE%E7%A0%B2%E5%8F%B0-03.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Bisha Fishing Port","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.145667,"lo":121.786,"d":4839,"ds":"The Bisha Fishing Port (traditional Chinese: 碧砂漁港; simplified Chinese: 碧砂渔港; pinyin: Bìshā Yúgǎng) is a harbor and fish market in Zhongzheng District, Keelung, Taiwan.","wpu":"Bisha Fishing Port","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Bisha_Fishing_Harbor-3.JPG/960px-Bisha_Fishing_Harbor-3.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Badouzi Fishing Port","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.1445,"lo":121.791361,"d":5325,"ds":"The Badouzi Fishing Port (traditional Chinese: 八斗子漁港; simplified Chinese: 八斗子渔港; pinyin: Bādǒuzi Yúgǎng) is a fish harbor in Zhongzheng District, Keelung, Taiwan.","wpu":"Badouzi Fishing Port","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/2021_Badouzi_Fishing_Port_iii.jpg/960px-2021_Badouzi_Fishing_Port_iii.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"National Museum of Marine Science and Technology","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.140556,"lo":121.798611,"d":5959,"ds":"The National Museum of Marine Science and Technology (NMMST; traditional Chinese: 國立海洋科技博物館; simplified Chinese: 国立海洋科技博物馆; pinyin: Guólì Hǎiyáng Kējì Bówùguǎn) is a museum of marine science and marine technology in Zhongzheng District, Keelung, Taiwan. It received 1,395,127 visits in 2016.","wpu":"National Museum of Marine Science and Technology","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/%E5%9F%BA%E9%9A%86%E6%B5%B7%E7%A7%91%E9%A4%A8_Keelung_Marine_Science_and_Technology_Museum_-_panoramio.jpg/960px-%E5%9F%BA%E9%9A%86%E6%B5%B7%E7%A7%91%E9%A4%A8_Keelung_Marine_Science_and_Technology_Museum_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Keelung Islet","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.192222,"lo":121.785556,"d":8024,"ds":"Keelung Islet (Chinese: 基隆嶼; pinyin: Jīlóng Yǔ; Wade–Giles: Chi1-lung2 Yü3, also 基隆島, in Taiwanese Hokkien: 雞籠杙/Ke-lâng-khit) is a small island in Zhongzheng District, Keelung, Taiwan and 4.9 km (3.0 mi) away from the Port of Keelung. It has an area of 27,005.593 m2 (0.010426918 mi2) or 23.91 ha (59.08 acres).","wpu":"Keelung Islet","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/%E5%9F%BA%E9%9A%86%E5%B6%BC_Keelong_Island_-_panoramio.jpg/960px-%E5%9F%BA%E9%9A%86%E5%B6%BC_Keelong_Island_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Shen'ao Fishing Port","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.135667,"lo":121.824583,"d":8519,"ds":"The Shen'ao Fishing Port (traditional Chinese: 深澳漁港; simplified Chinese: 深澳渔港; pinyin: Shēn'ào Yúgǎng) is a fishing harbor in Ruifang District, New Taipei, Taiwan.","wpu":"Shen'ao Fishing Port","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/%E6%B7%B1%E6%BE%B3%E6%BC%81%E6%B8%AF.JPG/960px-%E6%B7%B1%E6%BE%B3%E6%BC%81%E6%B8%AF.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Taiwan Coal Mine Museum","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.052778,"lo":121.773611,"d":9540,"ds":"The Taiwan Coal Mine Museum (traditional Chinese: 台灣煤礦博物館; simplified Chinese: 台湾煤矿博物馆; pinyin: Táiwān Méikuàng Bówùguǎn) is a museum about coal mining in Pingxi District, New Taipei City, Taiwan.","wpu":"Taiwan Coal Mine Museum","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/New_Pinghsi_Coal_Tunnel.JPG/960px-New_Pinghsi_Coal_Tunnel.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Taipei ( ), officially Taipei City, is the capital and a special municipality of Taiwan. Located in Northern Taiwan, Taipei City is an enclave of the municipality of New Taipei City that sits about 25 kilometres (16 mi) southwest of the northern port city of Keelung. Most of the city rests on the Taipei Basin, an ancient lakebed.","wpu":"Taipei","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Taipei_Skyline_2022.06.29.jpg/960px-Taipei_Skyline_2022.06.29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}